Here the first block p has wosize = pool_blocks - 1. That block p itself is free, and there are pool_blocks - 1 more free blocks after it. So Wosize means "the number of further free blocks after this one". p[1] = 0 is the next pointer, pointing at nothing because there are no more free blocks after the run.

