```
last_free_block is at some place. Its run extends over itself (the 1) plus Wosize_hp(last_free_block) more. If that run ends exactly at p, then they are contiguous. This is consistent with Wosize = number of further blocks.

3. The write-back on merge:
```c
*last_free_block = POOL_FREE_HEADER(Wosize_hp(last_free_block) + Wosize_hd(hd) + 1);
```
We take the last free block, which had Wosize_hp(last_free_block) further blocks. The new block p has Wosize_hd(hd) further blocks. Between the end of the old run and the new block there is the new block itself. So the number of further blocks from the old first block is Wosize_hp(last_free_block) + 1 (the new first block) + Wosize_hd(hd) (the ones after it). That + 1 is right and I was wrong to remove it. Good, I've now restored it.

