...
p += wh;
```
We are at the first free block. We move forward Wosize_hd(hd) blocks to get to the last free block in the run. Then the outer p += wh moves to the first block after the run. That is all correct.

So the sweep and the initialisation and the skipping are all mutually consistent. The only place that failed to agree was pool_allocate.

